  "lineage": "Two related rural song-dance forms of the Baracoa area at the eastern tip of Cuba, kept by campesino groups and regarded, with the changüí of nearby Guantánamo, as early forms from which son developed. Sung verses alternate with choral refrains over the repeated figures of the tres and small rural percussion such as güiro and maracas.",
